{"input": ["# SAP Technology and Sales Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key departments focusing on technology and sales, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to deliver innovative solutions and manage sales processes effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Trading Partner Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Trading Partner Management Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing trading partner relationships and ensuring seamless message interchange. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective trading partner management not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (49, 50, 51), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 01), (2025, 06, 08))]\n\n## Joule Capabilities and Integration\n\nJoule, SAP's AI copilot, has been integrated into various SAP systems, including SAP SuccessFactors Mobile apps and SAP Digital Manufacturing. This integration enables users to access Joule's capabilities, such as analytical insights and transactional use cases, to manage sales processes and provide comprehensive cash management capabilities. Joule's capabilities are crucial in maintaining SAP's operational efficiency and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (734, 735, 736, 737, 738), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 31), (2025, 06, 01))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Sales and Technology\n\nCollaboration between the Trading Partner Management and Joule Departments ensures that trading partner relationships are managed effectively and that sales processes are optimized. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating sales and technology strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with customer needs and market requirements. [Data: Sources (49, 734), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 01), (2025, 06, 08))]", "# Joule and SAP Integration Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of Joule and SAP integration, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide enhanced functionality and user experience. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Joule Integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\n\nJoule is now available in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition for various use cases, including navigation to a selection of apps in Sourcing and Procurement, Finance, Sales, Professional Services, and Public Sector industry. Viewing business data of purchase orders and purchase requisitions, outbound deliveries and sales orders, and information retrieval for all business areas are also supported. Note that an additional entitlement and authorization may be required to access Joule within SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition. Please consult your account executive for more information. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 06), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Joule Conversational Search Now Supported in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain\n\nJoule is now available in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain (SAP IBP) for informational use cases. This means that users have conversational access to the product documentation for SAP IBP. Just enter your query or question in plain natural language, and Joule searches the product documentation to find the answer. Joule summarizes the search results in the background. This summarization is then displayed to you as the answer to your question, along with the top search results. If you select the title link of a result, you're taken directly to the relevant topic on SAP Help Portal. [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 18), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## Document Grounding Capability - Support to Documents in Static HTML File Format\n\nThe document grounding capability now supports documents in static HTML file format. See Set Up Document Grounding. [Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 22), (2024, 11, 27))]\n\n## New Conversational Experience and Use Cases in Joule\n\nA new conversational experience featuring improved adaptive conversations and dialog management has been introduced. We’ve developed new use cases and have been upgrading the existing ones to take advantage of this new experience. For more details, refer to New Conversational Experience and Use Cases in Joule. [Data: Source (6), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 15), (2024, 11, 15))]\n\n## Joule Conversational Search Now Supported in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain\n\nJoule is now available in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain (SAP IBP) for informational use cases. This means that users have conversational access to the product documentation for SAP IBP. Just enter your query or question in plain natural language, and Joule searches the product documentation to find the answer. Joule summarizes the search results in the background. This summarization is then displayed to you as the answer to your question, along with the top search results. If you select the title link of a result, you're taken directly to the relevant topic on SAP Help Portal. [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 18), (2024, 10, 31))]", "# JUJU Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into JUJU's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2020, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, focusing on key components and their relationships. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Key Entities and Their Relationships\n\nThe report highlights key entities within SAP's technology landscape, including Joule, Identity Provisioning, and Connectivity. These entities are interconnected, with Joule being a crucial component in various use cases, such as conversational search and document grounding. The Identity Provisioning Department ensures secure access to these components, while Connectivity facilitates communication between them. Effective management of these relationships is vital for SAP's operational efficiency and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (271, 2007, 2008), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Joule's Expanding Capabilities\n\nJoule has been expanding its capabilities, with new features such as conversational search, document grounding, and authentication of requests. These enhancements have improved user experience and increased the component's versatility. Joule's integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition and SAP SuccessFactors has also been strengthened, enabling users to access a broader range of features and services. [Data: Sources (92, 95, 96), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning's Role in Security\n\nThe Identity Provisioning Department plays a critical role in ensuring secure access to SAP's technology components. Its support for OAuth certificate authentication and single logout (SLO) features has improved security and reduced the risk of unauthorized access. Effective identity management is essential for maintaining the integrity of SAP's systems and protecting customer data. [Data: Sources (2008, 2009), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their capabilities, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around December 2024.\n\n## OData Provisioning Capability\n\nThe OData Provisioning capability at SAP plays a pivotal role in exploring SAP Gateway services from SAP Business Suite systems and publishing them as OData end-points. This eliminates the need for an on-premise SAP Gateway server and enables users to run user-centric applications. Effective OData Provisioning not only simplifies data access but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 07), (2024, 12, 07))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management\n\nThe Trading Partner Management component at SAP ensures seamless interactions between trading partners by providing features such as resend/retry interchanges and software version updates. These features are crucial in maintaining the integrity of business transactions and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 07), (2024, 12, 07))]\n\n## Event Mesh Support for HTTP Protocol\n\nThe Event Mesh component at SAP now supports publishing and consuming messages using the HTTP protocol with the help of REST APIs. This feature is essential for integrating Event Mesh with other SAP services and enabling real-time data exchange. [Data: Source (4), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 06), (2024, 12, 06))]\n\n## Joule Integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\n\nJoule is now integrated with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition, enabling users to access Joule capabilities for various use cases such as navigation, viewing business data, and information retrieval. This integration is crucial for streamlining business processes and improving user experience. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 06), (2024, 12, 06))]\n\n## Joule Conversational Search in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain\n\nJoule is now available in SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain (SAP IBP) for informational use cases, enabling users to access product documentation through conversational search. This feature is essential for improving user experience and reducing the time spent on searching for information. [Data: Source (8), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 18), (2024, 10, 31))]", "# SAP Build and SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Overview as of March 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Build and SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing, highlighting key features, collaborations, and insights into the organizational framework of these components within SAP. The information is relevant to the company's operations around March 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Features and Enhancements\n\nSAP Build offers various features and enhancements, including the Resources feature, Lobby UI Improvements, and Import Project Enhancements. These features aim to improve user experience and streamline project management. The introduction of the Resources feature and Lobby UI Improvements enhances transparency and organization within the lobby, while the Import Project Enhancements provide timely updates and ensure a smooth import experience. [Data: Sources (133, 134, 135), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 15), (2024, 03, 15))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Enhancements\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has introduced various enhancements, including Configure Omnichannel Promotion Pricing app enhancements, Reusing a Merchandise Set, and Security Recommendation on Extensibility. These enhancements aim to improve the user experience and provide more flexibility in configuring promotion pricing. The Configure Omnichannel Promotion Pricing app enhancements include renaming of the Padding Configurations section, removal of the Padding Character field, and additional settings for Identifier Formats. [Data: Sources (3297, 3298, 3299), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 13))]\n\n## Intercomponent Collaboration\n\nCollaboration between SAP Build and SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing is essential for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced intercomponent cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological standards. [Data: Sources (133, 3297), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 15), (2024, 03, 13))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of March 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology as of March 2024, focusing on various components such as Cloud Build Service, SAP Build, Cloud Application Programming Model, and more. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development around this period.\n\n## Cloud Build Service Updates\n\nThe Cloud Build Service has undergone several updates, including the addition of new supported versions, such as March 2024 (2305 PL14) and February 2024 (2305 PL12). These updates aim to improve the service's functionality and compatibility. The updates are essential for developers and users who rely on the Cloud Build Service for their projects. [Data: Sources (362, 335), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 29))]\n\n## SAP Build Enhancements\n\nSAP Build has introduced several enhancements, including the Lobby feature, which provides a clear indication of when a project import is underway. Additionally, the Store feature now includes a Deprecated tag to help users identify packages that are no longer receiving updates. These enhancements aim to improve the user experience and streamline project management. [Data: Sources (3291, 3294), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 15), (2024, 03, 15))]\n\n## Cloud Application Programming Model Updates\n\nThe Cloud Application Programming Model has received updates, including the March release, which introduced revised cookbooks and Java documentation. These updates aim to improve the model's functionality and compatibility. The updates are essential for developers and users who rely on the Cloud Application Programming Model for their projects. [Data: Sources (3213), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 03, 28))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2024, focusing on the company's efforts to maintain its technological superiority.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (4045, 4046, 4047), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 17), (2023, 10, 19))]\n\n## SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Capabilities\n\nThe SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3761), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 07, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Build Process Automation and SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Departments, established in Q2 2023, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3763, 3764), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 07, 12))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Updates as of November 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes in SAP's technology and finance departments, highlighting the importance of interdepartmental collaboration and the impact of these updates on the company's operations and compliance.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (651, 652), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Legal Compliance and Governance\n\nThe Legal Compliance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (652), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2023, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (651, 652), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Technology Updates\n\nSAP has made significant updates to its technology, including the release of the Eventing module, updates to the SAP Java Buildpack, and the introduction of new features in SAP Datasphere. These updates aim to improve the company's operational efficiency and compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (652, 653, 654), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 06), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Finance Updates\n\nSAP has also made updates to its finance department, including changes to the default value displayed for task descriptions in the Advanced Financial Closing module and the introduction of new features in the SAP Internet Transaction Server. These updates aim to improve the company's financial management and compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (652, 655, 656), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 27), (2023, 11, 16))]", "# SAP and KPI Overview as of 2023-12-12\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components focusing on process automation, highlighting how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and streamline processes effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2023-12-12.\n\n## SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in automating business processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous process automation. Effective process automation not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2023, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation and Governance\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the process automation standards set by organizational bodies. Their focus on process automation, noted starting 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex processes and business agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high process automation standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 12, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Process Automation\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation and SAP Build Process Automation Departments, established in 2023, ensures that process automation strategies are effective and that compliance measures consider operational risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating process automation with operational strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with operational requirements. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 12, 12))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of December 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of December 2023. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates in 2023, including the introduction of new features such as event triggers, export health metrics, and manage traces. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the overall efficiency of the system. [Data: Sources (3748, 3749, 3750, 3751, 3752, 3753, 3754, 3755, 3756, 3757, 3758, 3759, 3760, 3761, 3762, 3763, 3764, 3765, 3766, 3767, 3768, 3651, 3652, 3653, 3654, 3655, 3656, 3657, 3658, 3659, 3660), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 12), (2024, 01, 16))]\n\n## SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation has also seen significant updates in 2023, including the introduction of new features such as error management, core SDK, and record web and windows applications with the enhanced recorder. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the overall efficiency of the system. [Data: Sources (3759, 3761, 3762, 3763, 3764, 3765, 3766, 3767, 3768, 3651, 3652, 3653, 3654, 3655, 3656, 3657, 3658, 3659, 3660), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 12), (2024, 01, 16))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has seen significant updates in 2023, including the introduction of new features such as branding and layout, regular upgrade, and upgrade dates. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the overall efficiency of the system. [Data: Sources (3652, 3653, 3654, 3655, 3656, 3657, 3658, 3659, 3660), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 16), (2024, 02, 20))]", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's Variant Configuration and Pricing key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide effective pricing and configuration solutions. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Variant Configuration Operational Scope\n\nThe Variant Configuration component at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating configuration risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential configuration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective configuration management not only prevents configuration anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (813, 814, 815, 816, 817), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service component at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating pricing risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential pricing pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective pricing management not only prevents pricing anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (518, 520, 1481, 1482, 1483), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Variant Configuration and Pricing departments, established in Q2 2025, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2020, 01, 01, 2020, 01, 2020, 07, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and development around this time.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\n\n## Legal Compliance and Governance\n\nThe Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\n\n## SAP BTP Technology Updates\n\nSAP BTP has undergone significant updates in 2024, including the deprecation of weak client certificate chains, the removal of .NET, Ruby, and R buildpacks, and the addition of new regions and IP addresses. These changes aim to enhance security, improve compliance, and expand the platform's capabilities. [Data: Sources (3382, 3385, 3384), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## SAP Business Application Studio Updates\n\nSAP Business Application Studio has received several updates in 2024, including the addition of new features such as calculation view refactoring, hierarchy copying, and window function copying. These updates aim to improve the development experience and enhance the platform's capabilities. [Data: Sources (461, 462, 463, 464, 465), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Continuous Integration and Delivery Updates\n\nContinuous Integration and Delivery has undergone several updates in 2024, including the addition of new features such as Bitbucket Cloud authentication and changes to certificate-based authentication. These updates aim to improve the development experience and enhance the platform's capabilities. [Data: Sources (467, 468), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations and maintenance.\n\n## Cloud Connector Updates\n\nThe Cloud Connector has undergone several updates in 2024, including the addition of new IP addresses to SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS) [Data: Sources (3842, 3843), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]. These updates aim to enhance the platform's security and connectivity features. The Cloud Connector 2.16.1 release also addressed several bug fixes, including issues with LDAP role names, passwords, and subaccount selection [Data: Sources (3843), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))].\n\n## TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining Ciphers Deleted\n\nAs announced on October 19, 2023, the following TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining (CBC) Ciphers have been removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment for the region eu20 [Data: Sources (3841), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2024, 12, 31))]. This change aims to enhance the platform's security features and prevent potential vulnerabilities. Older clients might be affected by this change, and users are advised to check and ensure that their clients are supporting one of the following TLS 1.2 ciphers that are still supported [Data: Sources (3841), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2024, 12, 31))].\n\n## New Regions and Features\n\nSAP BTP has introduced several new regions and features in 2024, including the addition of Brazil (São Paulo) and Australia (Sydney) as new regions for use with enterprise accounts and Partner Test, Demo, and Development accounts [Data: Sources (2230, 2231), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]. The platform has also introduced new features, such as the SAP Datasphere connector, the SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database connector, and the SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management connector [Data: Sources (2222, 2223, 2224), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))].", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2024. The information is relevant to the company's operations and strategic planning.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1701, 1702), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Legal Compliance and Governance\n\nThe Legal Compliance Department ensures that all SAP BTP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1703), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1705, 1706), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded multiple times in 2024, with the latest upgrade being on 2024-12-12. These upgrades have improved the overall stability and security of the service. [Data: Sources (1608, 1428, 1763), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has been updated multiple times in 2024, with the latest update being on 2024-12-12. These updates have improved the overall stability and security of the service. [Data: Sources (1429, 1766), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Updates\n\nCloud Logging has been updated multiple times in 2024, with the latest update being on 2024-12-12. These updates have improved the overall stability and security of the service. [Data: Sources (1764, 1765), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_8cd10678bf6e8ec6b